{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785993644401772001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"veiny-trout-brink","assignee":"","attestations":{"plan-review":{"algorithm":"HMAC-SHA256","author":"Iso Tester","head_sha":"0f4e5dca9313e6ed35d47c85508d38d6fc535730","key_id":"412fa5372ad877e0","kind":"plan-review","manifest":["plan-review: PASS","ticket: 586c-bfb0-8206-4209","material: 368bf1384524eaeb","model: claude-opus-4-8","runner: pydantic_ai","blocking: 0","advisory: 10","regver: 0dbaa5513314ac56","verified-at-sha:c48162ca6b1d8fb052f8e10934a9d24976f5b1d7","dep 757b1eac70d365ceee085b2414d2a2f33277fb27f07abe31dc02b75f0966c34c src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py","dep a04bdb77b14d68032f97693c841ab8966e5fe0bdbc3325465a5488b03a93e011 src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py","dep 92a0c5d019626037bc7eaf1480e5c55c96af47b9a25094866e649f61f4206bbc src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py","dep 257ea233d968a1e1db1380c08d2b09d11db20e0f74c652225971baefa61196a7 src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py","dep e6e51c3cf15733ef56d882ae208b094d164e82657a8ca6937c2db6593c55b2cd src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_ops.py","dep 44567b879616445fa1e4cac488c8b42e6a95a9de1da899fbada9c3dcee25b781 tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_workflow.py"],"signature":"ae8bff1ac328cbf37ff07b40735e1f007c2383c9dabd5f1a8a8a40b9a9a49ec2","signed_at":1782679711862658000}},"author":"Iso Tester","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":8},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Iso Tester","body":"Plan-review advisory triage (PASS + signed). The advisories correctly flag that the ticket's `LLMConfig.from_env()` call-site index is STALE + INCOMPLETE — implementation must NOT trust the listed line numbers:\n\n- STALE LINES: workflow_ops.py:329 is now a COMMENT (my #77 / drag-gripe-brake merge shifted lines); :113 likewise moved. Implementation will `grep -n \"LLMConfig.from_env(\" src/rebar/llm/plan_review/ src/rebar/llm/workflow/` and fix EVERY site, not the listed numbers (A1/E4/G1G2).\n- MISSED SITE (critical T8/G6/A1): `plan_review_verify_inputs` (workflow_ops.py ~238) calls `_verifier_cfg(LLMConfig.from_env(...)).model` to size the verify request — must receive the resolved cfg/model identity too.\n- gate_ops.completion_reconcile (~104) calls from_env ONLY for `cfg.repo_path` (not model/runner) — thread repo_path (or the resolved cfg identity) through inputs; document that this site needs repo_path, not just model/runner (G1G2).\n- AC1 TEST (E5/E6/F1): add a DETERMINISTIC test that a caller passing an explicit `config=` (non-default model/runner) sees it in BOTH the LLM calls AND the verdict's model/runner fields — currently AC4 only says \"existing tests pass\". Will add to tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_workflow.py.\n- CONTRACT (T5e): the new \"ops read model/runner identity from ctx.inputs (threaded once at the run boundary) instead of re-deriving from env\" is a workflow contract — document it at the produce_* boundary + the ops, mirroring the ticket_id threading pattern. Keep StepContext config-agnostic (per ticket scope).\n\nNet: scope is broader than the ticket's line index implied (more from_env sites + the verify_inputs sizing path). No blocking issues. Will claim + implement after c38b (tarry-creep-range / PR #79) closes.","timestamp":1782679751669466001}],"created_at":1782605232128463001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[],"description":"Workflow gate ops re-resolve `LLMConfig.from_env()` independently instead of receiving the caller's resolved config, producing a DOCUMENTED correctness divergence: a library caller passing an explicit non-default `config=` has it honored for the LLM calls but the workflow verdict's `model`/`runner` fields still reflect the env config (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py:78-79`).\n\n## Why\nConfig resolution is a cross-cutting concern that should resolve once per run, not once per op. The current scatter silently ignores part of a caller's explicit configuration — a reliability/correctness gap for library/MCP consumers.\n\n## What / files\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py:113,329`, `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_ops.py:60,104`, `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py:89` — stop calling `LLMConfig.from_env(...)` per op.\n- Resolve `cfg` once at the run boundary (`gate_dispatch.produce_*` / `review_plan`) and pass the `runner`/`model` identity into the ops as workflow `inputs` (the pattern already used for `ticket_id`), so ops read it from `ctx.inputs` rather than re-deriving from env. Keep `StepContext` config-agnostic (`executor.py:107-120`).\n\n## Scope\nIn: single-resolution + thread model/runner identity through inputs; remove the documented divergence note. Out: redesigning `StepContext` to carry the full `LLMConfig` type.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A caller passing an explicit `config=` sees that model/runner reflected in BOTH the LLM calls and the verdict's `model`/`runner` fields.\n- [ ] No op calls `LLMConfig.from_env()` after the run boundary resolves it.\n- [ ] The divergence caveat at `plan_review/__init__.py:78-79` is removed (no longer true).\n- [ ] Existing plan-review/completion gate tests still pass.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py","reason":"resolve cfg once at the run boundary (produce_*) and thread model/runner identity into workflow inputs"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py","reason":"stop per-op LLMConfig.from_env(); read model/runner from ctx.inputs"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_ops.py","reason":"stop per-op LLMConfig.from_env(); read resolved identity from inputs"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py","reason":"stop per-op LLMConfig.from_env()"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py","reason":"remove the documented model/runner divergence caveat"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_workflow.py","reason":"test: explicit config= reflected in verdict model/runner"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","5ca8-5993-ca83-40f1"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"5ca8-5993-ca83-40f1","parent_status_uuid":"65b6689f-5b31-4c97-83b8-45f2e3b21e3a","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["audit-2026-06-27","oss-remediation"],"ticket_id":"586c-bfb0-8206-4209","ticket_type":"task","title":"Honor caller's explicit LLMConfig in workflow gate ops","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["31a45b5e-b39f-41ea-8daf-aea1720e54d5","287107a7-b975-4b4d-a8bb-047ff10377f1","93462e87-1acf-4d42-8c8a-5c1c0ac5dc15","bf8f36a5-8fd7-4c7a-a0de-583396dec012","e3b40f53-8d49-4e28-b0b1-c77d259c5fd6","cc4a913f-b590-4263-9776-f4f9a7cee0d7","65b6689f-5b31-4c97-83b8-45f2e3b21e3a","4940e5f6-5fd1-47cb-8845-5cbbd431075d","638c680a-0882-4b96-bb60-3108c16f479f"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785993644401772001,"uuid":"c743228f-9753-47b3-a92b-b4a3b1223d97"}